### 1. Health check 200 means successful read
GET http://localhost:8081/api/health


### 2, Get all course offerings
GET http://localhost:8081/api/course-offerings


### 3. Get a specific course offering
GET http://localhost:8081/api/course-offerings/CO001


### 4. Get a course that doesn't exist
GET http://localhost:8081/api/course-offerings/O999


### 5. Create a new course offering 201 means successful creation
POST http://localhost:8081/api/course-offerings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courseTitle": "Spring Boot Fundamentals",
  "instructorName": "Mr Fernando",
  "startDate": "2026-08-15",
  "capacity": 25
}


### 6. Create an invalid course 400 means bad request
POST http://localhost:8081/api/course-offerings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courseTitle": "",
  "instructorName": "",
  "startDate": "",
  "capacity": 0
}

### Get all bookings
GET http://localhost:8081/api/bookings


### Create a valid booking
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EV001",
  "participantName": "Rahim Gonzalez",
  "participantEmail": "rahim@example.com",
  "seats": 2
}


### Get one booking (use the id returned above)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/bookings/BK001


### Create a booking with missing fields
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "",
  "participantName": "",
  "participantEmail": "",
  "seats": 0
}


### Create a booking with an invalid event ID
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EV999",
  "participantName": "Rahim Gonzalez",
  "participantEmail": "rahim@example.com",
  "seats": 2
}


### Create a booking with too many seats
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EV002",
  "participantName": "Rahim Gonzalez",
  "participantEmail": "rahim@example.com",
  "seats": 100
}


### Cancel a booking (challenge task)
DELETE http://localhost:8081/api/bookings/BK001
